880 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Summary: Join Amy C. Oliver, FRAS for a deep dive into the Smithsonian Institution's Fred Lawrence Whipple Observatory. Home to one of the largest single mirror telescopes on ground, the MMT and the only gamma-ray array in North America, the Whipple Observatory searches the visible and invisible Universe on roughly 300 clear nights to understand supernovae, galaxy behaviors, stellar metallicity, exoplanets, and TeV gamma rays.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
