/T (Astronomers using the James Webb Space Telescope \(JWST\) have identified a red supergiant star moments before its explosive end, buried beneath a thick shroud of carbon-rich dust. The star, which later became supernova SN 2025pht in the galaxy NGC 1637, about 32 million light-years away, marks the first time a star of this kind has been directly observed before its death.   )
